Spooky.

32
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:13,580
So, okay, we've got two interesting words here, ultra and spooky.

33
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:16,320
Now spooky is scary, right?

34
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:16,940
It's a little bit scary.

35
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:22,560
It maybe makes you feel a little bit uncomfortable or maybe it makes you feel a little bit scared.

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,040
Okay, so not very scared.

37
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,760
Not super scared.

38
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:27,680
But ultra spooky.

39
00:02:28,410 --> 00:02:32,910
So ultra is another way of saying super or very or really spooky.

40
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:34,970
So if it's ultra spooky then it's...

41
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:35,830
Very scary.

42
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:36,330
Okay.

43
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,840
All right, so our next word.

44
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:43,650
They said that in the house there is a ghost haunting the house.

45
00:02:44,170 --> 00:02:47,090
Okay, there is a ghost haunting his house.

46
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:50,030
Okay, so the verb to haunt.

47
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,440
Okay, to haunt.

48
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:57,940
So the ghost is coming to the house frequently and not letting them live in peace.

49
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:02,100
When a ghost haunts something, it visits it often and scares it.

50
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:02,720
Exactly.

51
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:09,400
Now, they were all afraid and they didn't want to go in and so Wilma called everyone cowards.

52
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,300
Stop being such cowards.

53
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,600
Cowards.

54
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:13,900
So, a coward.

55
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,440
A coward is a person that's not brave.

56
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:19,070
A person who's scared of everything.

57
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:19,710
Exactly.

58
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,320
So, they were being cowards.

59
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:25,320
They were afraid so that's why they didn't want to go in.

60
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:30,960
Well, speaking of being afraid, Shabby said, I'm getting goose bumps.

61
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,960
Goose bumps.

62
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,080
To get goose bumps.

63
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,240
All right, to get goose bumps.

64
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:45,590
Now, goose bumps, it may sound a little bit strange but it's very easy when you're scared or maybe you're cold, the skin on your arms or on your back, it gets a little bit bumpy.

65
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:47,830
So your skin looks like chicken skin.

66
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:55,250
Exactly, chicken skin and that's actually how we call it in Spanish, chicken skin but this is goose bumps so I guess it's kind of similar.

67
00:03:55,470 --> 00:03:55,730
A goose.

68
00:03:56,210 --> 00:03:57,530
Yeah, same idea.

69
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,360
Goose bumps.

70
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:03,110
All right and finally, Scruffy said, Shabby is a scaredy cat.

71
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:04,730
A scaredy cat.

72
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:05,610
A scaredy cat.

73
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,020
You're a scaredy cat.

74
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:10,040
Well, a scaredy cat is not really a cat, right?

75
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,320
No, no, no.

76
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,720
It's a person who's afraid of everything.

77
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,320
Okay.

78
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,340
Similar to a coward.

79
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,090
But more informal.

80
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,120
Much more informal.

81
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:21,550
So somebody is a scaredy cat and I think even a little bit more juvenile.

82
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:22,510
As adults.

83
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,240
So children use it.

84
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,990
Yeah, as adults, you wouldn't say he's a scaredy cat.

85
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:27,770
All right, great.

